  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8123665448dc45ddabbbff513c0aa9e1",
      "statement": "Service classes (PaymentService, AuthorizationService, RefundService, ClientService, ClientActivityService, ConnectorMsgService, ErrorService) provide a thin stateless facade over the Oracle database; each public method builds ordered input/output parameter maps and delegates execution to DBProcedureUtil.execute, then throws OracleException when the procedure's response code does not match the expected HTTP status.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/common/service/PaymentService.java#L28-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40449bdb579053551ca9dedfca71f6fcd4efcc43d943435932939bf23d12eaf1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/common/util/DBProcedureUtil.java#L20-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f68eaaca59afd287f15e6e974a9effb504095bad8600e2a8379811e55fd3fcb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86020daa25ab4d7b8275cddf224b3aa4",
      "statement": "The Main entry point creates a single HikariDataSource for the Oracle database and injects it at startup into the public dataSource fields of PaymentService, AuthorizationService, and RefundService, and into DB via DB.setDataSource; other services (ClientActivityService, ConnectorMsgService, ClientService, ErrorService) expose setDataSource methods instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/Main.java#L42-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ccea24882608d364a582c78a617bfd07974dff22853077f839ff6536e1e84e82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c3c5a55a891040e995459ecc70458efe",
      "statement": "PaymentService.insert creates a payment record by calling PKG_PAYMENT.payment_insert, masking the instrument number via AppUtil.getInstrumentMask before storage, and returns the formatted created row; PaymentService.update records the PSP response and state via PKG_PAYMENT.payment_update; PaymentService.get retrieves a payment by connector ID via PKG_PAYMENT.payment_get.",
      "evidence": [
        {
