    {
      "id": "claim_1fec2e24a8ee4e10af486de2f76510c2",
      "statement": "All service methods follow a uniform six-step database interaction pattern: build input map, declare output parameter types and names, call DBProcedureUtil.execute with the procedure constant from ProcedurePool, check the response code against the expected HTTP status, and format the first RESPONSE_DATA row. This requires any new domain operation to also add its procedure constant to ProcedurePool.",
